## 2. Core Contract Invariants (`CT1`–`CT10`, Mandatory Compliance)

Every rule in [`references/base-rules.md`]({{base_rules_ref}}) (`CT1`–`CT10`) is **mandatory compliance** — never invent per-rule severity columns or mark any invariant as `"not adopted"`:

| ID | Rule Summary | Primary Reference |
|---|---|---|
| `CT1` | **Contract Snapshot Is Reviewable Evidence** (`{{snapshot_path}}` committed & checked in CI) | [03-snapshot-handshake-and-review.md]({{ref_03}}) |
| `CT2` | **Separate Input and Output Schemas** (no shared ORM/Domain entity on the wire; strict input validation) | [01-conventions-schemas-and-idempotency.md]({{ref_01}}) |
| `CT3` | **Single Structured Error Envelope** (`{{error_envelope_model}}` across all 4xx/5xx responses) | [01-conventions-schemas-and-idempotency.md]({{ref_01}}) |
| `CT4` | **Explicit Status Codes & Response Contracts** (`200`/`201`/`204`/`400`/`401`/`403`/`404`/`409`/`422`/`429`) | [01-conventions-schemas-and-idempotency.md]({{ref_01}}) |
| `CT5` | **Explicit Authentication, Authorization Scopes, and Tenant/Object Ownership (Anti-IDOR)** | [02-auth-scopes-and-compatibility.md]({{ref_02}}) |
| `CT6` | **Bounded Pagination, Deterministic Sort, and Allow-Listed Filtering** | [01-conventions-schemas-and-idempotency.md]({{ref_01}}) |
| `CT7` | **Additive Changes by Default; Breaking Changes Require Decision Record (`D-NN`)** | [02-auth-scopes-and-compatibility.md]({{ref_02}}) |
| `CT8` | **Explicit Deprecation & Versioning Policy (One-Version Rule Within a Major Prefix)** | [02-auth-scopes-and-compatibility.md]({{ref_02}}) |
| `CT9` | **Deterministic Operation IDs, Tags, and Cross-Repo Handshake (`api_contract.json`)** | [03-snapshot-handshake-and-review.md]({{ref_03}}) |
| `CT10` | **Idempotency & Safe Retries for State-Changing Operations (`Idempotency-Key`)** | [01-conventions-schemas-and-idempotency.md]({{ref_01}}) |

