## 4. Deterministic CLI Verification Gates (`PASS` / `FAIL`)

All automated contract checks report strictly **`PASS`** or **`FAIL`** (`NOT_RUN`, `BLOCKED`, and `UNVERIFIED` never count as `PASS`):

| Gate | Command | Pass Criterion |
|---|---|---|
| **G1 — Snapshot Drift Gate** | `{{snapshot_export_cmd}} && git diff --exit-code {{snapshot_path}}` | Exit `0` (`PASS`) — committed snapshot matches live code |
| **G2 — Compatibility Diff Gate** | `{{snapshot_diff_cmd}}` | Exit `0` (`PASS`) — zero unapproved breaking changes without `D-NN` |
| **G3 — Unbounded List / Raw Dict Scan** | `rg -n "{{raw_wire_pattern}}" {{router_glob}}` | Zero matches (`PASS`) |
| **G4 — Contract Schema Test Suite** | `{{contract_test_cmd}}` | Exit `0` (`PASS`) |
